-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Drawing engine
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/lib/iso/core.js is adapted from Colorfigures by April Zhu
(https://april-zhu.com/colorfigures). Colorfigures grew from her ISO-GLOW
(https://isoglow.dev), which builds on iso-figure by Tolga Cohce
(https://github.com/MrBongoC/ai-iso-skill). All are MIT licensed. The full
license text is in src/lib/iso/LICENSE.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms followed (no source copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- The byte-level BPE tokenizer in src/lib/lm/ follows the algorithm of minbpe
  by Andrej Karpathy (https://github.com/karpathy/minbpe), MIT.
- Larkspur mini, the tiny model in scripts/train/ and src/lib/lm/model.ts, is
  shaped after nanoGPT by Andrej Karpathy (https://github.com/karpathy/nanoGPT),
  MIT.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models used to compute committed data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 (Apache-2.0)
  computed the retrieval embeddings and scores in public/data/index/.
- The GPT-2 tokenizer (Xenova/gpt2, MIT) and the o200k_base tokenizer
  (Xenova/gpt-4o, from OpenAI's tiktoken, MIT) produced the recorded tokens in
  data/tokens/.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recorded model outputs
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Some chapters show model replies recorded ahead of time through NVIDIA's API
and labelled as recorded on the page. The recordings came from:

- openai/gpt-oss-20b and openai/gpt-oss-120b (Apache-2.0)
- nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b (NVIDIA Open Model License)

